<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina and Chile reach mining accords.</title>
<headline>Argentina and Chile reach mining accords.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRE 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina and Chile have reached final agreement on separate protocols to allow two mining projects to operate across the countries' Andean mountain border, Argentina's Industry Secretariat said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The two protocols will allow the Pachon copper project, owned 50-percent by Canada's Cambior Inc, and the Pascua-Lama gold project, being developed by Canada's Barrick Gold Corp, to go ahead, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The protocols will be signed in Argentina in the next few days.</p>
<p>((Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
